{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>who sits on his throne.</b> The one fit to sit on his throne after him. And He mentioned the most exalted of all Egypt, who is the son of their lord, for all are slaves to him; and the lowliest of all, the firstborn of the maidservant, who is a slave." "And the meaning of \"who is behind the millstones\" — he is a grinder, as in \"and he became a grinder in the prison house\" (Judges 16:21). And I have already said that the prophets do not guard the words but only the meanings, for the word הגמאיני (Genesis 24:17) and השקיני (ibid. ibid. 45), and זכור and שמור, and שוא and שקר, לא תחמוד and לא תתאוה are equivalent in meaning. And I will yet speak of this in the prayer of Moses. And behold, the firstborn of the maidservant is like the firstborn of the captive, for the captured woman is a maidservant, and they sleep in the pit-house at night according to the custom of prisoners, as Joseph mentioned: \"for they put me in the pit\" (Genesis 40:15)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:33:22.916273583Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}